    "physical_description": "Shoulder cloth (<i>selendang</i>) of plain-weave cotton decorated in batik using a hand-drawn wax-resist technique on mill-woven cloth. The design comprises red and blue diamond-shaped stylised floral motifs, framed by green and yellow borders.",
    "summary": "This batik <i>selendang</i> or shoulder-cloth  dating to about 1900, was made in Cirebon on the north coast of Java, for the south-eastern Sumatran market. Its design of red and blue diamond-like stylized flowers with a green and yellow border was made using hand-drawn wax resist on mill cotton cloth",
